>ISM</b><b><sup>®</sup></b>&nbsp;<b><i>Services PMI</i></b><b><i><sup>®</sup></i></b><b><i> Report</i></b>&nbsp;data is seasonally adjusted for the Business Activity, New Orders, Employment and Prices indexes. <b>ISM</b><b><sup>®</sup></b>&nbsp;<b><i>Manufacturing PMI</i></b><b><i><sup>®</sup></i></b><b><i> Report</i></b> data is seasonally adjusted for New Orders, Production, Employment and Inventories indexes.<br />*Number of months moving in current direction.</p><p><u><b>COMMODITIES REPORTED UP/DOWN IN PRICE, AND IN SHORT SUPPLY</b></u></p><p><b>Commodities Up in Price<br /></b>Aluminum; Chicken; Copper (11); Diesel Fuel (8); Equipment/Equipment Parts; Food Products (3); Fuel (9); Gasoline (9); High Density Polyethylene (HDPE); Insurance; Labor (2); Labor — Construction; Memory Products (10); Petroleum Based Products (6); Software — Licensing (9); Software — Maintenance; Steel Products (7); Vehicles; and Wire and Cable (2).</p><p><b>Commodities Down in Price<br /></b>None.</p><p><b>Commodities in Short Supply<br /></b>Computers and Related Products (2); Memory Components (10);&nbsp;and Wire and Cable (5).</p><p>Note: The number of consecutive months the commodity is listed is indicated after each item.<br />*Indicates both up and down in price.</p><p class="prntac"><b>OCTOBER 2026 SERVICES INDEX SUMMARIES</b></p><p><u><b>Services PMI</b></u><b><sup>®</sup></b>&nbsp;<br />In October, the Services PMI<sup>®</sup>&nbsp;registered 54.5 percent, 0.2 percentage point above its 12-month moving average of 54.3 percent. A reading above 50 percent indicates the services sector economy is generally expanding; below 50 percent indicates it is generally contracting.</p><p>A Services PMI<sup>®</sup>&nbsp;above 48.1 percent, over time, generally indicates an expansion of the overall economy.&nbsp;Therefore, the October Services PMI<sup>®</sup>&nbsp;indicates the overall economy is expanding for the 77th straight month.&nbsp;Miller says, "The past relationship between the Services PMI<sup>®</sup>&nbsp;and the overall economy indicates that the Services PMI<sup>®</sup>&nbsp;for October (54.5 percent) corresponds to a 2-percentage point increase in real gross domestic product (GDP) on an annualized basis."</p><p><b>SERVICES PMI</b><b><sup>®</sup></b>&nbsp;<b>HISTORY</b></p><div><div class="divOverflow"><div class="table-responsive"><table><tr><td class="prngen9" colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p class="prnml4"><span class="prnews_span"><b><i>Month</i></b></span></p></td><td class="prngen2" colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p class="prnml4"><span class="prnews_span"><b>Services PMI</b><b><sup>®</sup></b></span></p></td><td class="prngen2" colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p class="prnml4"><span class="prnews_span"><b><i>Month</i></b></span></p></td><td class="prngen2" colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p class="prnml4"><span class="prnews_span"><b>Services PMI</b><b><sup>®</sup></b></span></p></td></tr><tr><td class="prngen9" colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p class="prnml4"><span class="prnews_span">Oct 2026</span></p></td><td class="prngen2" colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p class="prnml4"><span class="prnews_span">54.5</span></p></td><td class="prngen2" colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p class="prnml4"><span class="prnews_span">Apr 2026</span></p></td><td class="prngen2" colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p class="prnml4"><span class="prnews_span">53.6</span></p></td></tr><tr><td class="prngen9" colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p class="prnml4"><span class="prnews_span">Sep 2026</span></p></td><td class="prngen2" colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p class="prnml4"><span class="prnews_span">54.9</span></p></td><td class="prngen2" colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p class="prnml4"><span class="prnews_span">Mar 2026</span></p></td><td class="prngen2" colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p class="prnml4"><span class="prnews_span">54.0</span></p></td></tr><tr><td class="prngen9" colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p class="prnml4"><span class="prnews_span">Aug 2026</span></p></td><td class="prngen2" colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p class="prnml4"><span class="prnew