on in October; the reading of 53.8 percent is&nbsp;2.7 percentage points lower than the&nbsp;56.5 percent recorded in September. October's reading is 2.9 percentage points below the index's 12-month moving average of 56.7 percent, the same as September's reading. Comments from respondents include: "Very good movie content drove higher volumes" and "Increase in business activity from new and existing customers."</p><p>The 13 industries reporting an increase in business activity for the month of October — listed in order — are:&nbsp;Arts, Entertainment &amp; Recreation; Finance &amp; Insurance; Transportation &amp; Warehousing; Information; Wholesale Trade; Accommodation &amp; Food Services; Other Services; Educational Services; Retail Trade; Management of Companies &amp; Support Services; Public Administration; Utilities; and Professional, Scientific &amp; Technical Services. The two industries reporting a decrease in business activity in the month of October are: Construction; and Real Estate, Rental &amp; Leasing.</p><div><div class="divOverflow"><div class="table-responsive"><table><tr><td class="prngen9" colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p class="prnml4"><span class="prnews_span">Business Activity</span></p></td><td class="prngen2" colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p class="prnml4"><span class="prnews_span">%Higher</span></p></td><td class="prngen2" colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p class="prnml4"><span class="prnews_span">%Same</span></p></td><td class="prngen2" colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p class="prnml4"><span class="prnews_span">%Lower</span></p></td><td class="prngen2" colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p class="prnml4"><span class="prnews_span">Index</span></p></td></tr><tr><td class="prngen9" colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p class="prnml4"><span class="prnews_span">Oct 2026</span></p></td><td class="prngen2" colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p class="prnml4"><span class="prnews_span">20.8</span></p></td><td class="prngen2" colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p class="prnml4"><span class="prnews_span">67.8</span></p></t