panded for a second consecutive month in October, as the index registered 51.4 percent. The reading is up 1.3 percentage points from the September figure of 50.1 percent and is 2.1 percentage points above the index's 12-month average of 49.3 percent. Comments from respondents include: "Increasing employment to support business growth and new contract awards" and "Less people, more work equals frustration."</p><p>The six industries reporting an increase in employment in October — listed in order — are:&nbsp;Transportation &amp; Warehousing; Retail Trade; Real Estate, Rental &amp; Leasing; Accommodation &amp; Food Services; Utilities; and Wholesale Trade. The seven industries reporting a decrease in employment in October — listed in order — are: Management of Companies &amp; Support Services; Health Care &amp; Social Assistance; Other Services; Mining; Construction; Educational Services; and Public Administration.</p><div><div class="divOverflow"><div class="table-responsive"><table><tr><td class="prngen9" colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p class="prnml4"><span class="prnews_span">Employment</span></p></td><td class="prngen2" colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p class="prnml4"><span class="prnews_span">%Higher</span></p></td><td class="prngen2" colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p class="prnml4"><span class="prnews_span">%Same</span></p></td><td class="prngen2" colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p class="prnml4"><span class="prnews_span">%Lower</span></p></td><td class="prngen2" colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p class="prnml4"><span class="prnews_span">Index</span></p></td></tr><tr><td class="prngen9" colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p class="prnml4"><span class="prnews_span">Oct 2026</span></p></td><td class="prngen2" colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p class="prnml4"><span class="prnews_span">16.6</span></p></td><td class="prngen2" colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p class="prnml4"><span class="prnews_span">69.9</span></p></td><td class="prngen2" colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p class="prnml4"><span class="prnews_span">13.5</span></p></td><t