"1"><p class="prnml4"><span class="prnews_span">50.9</span></p></td></tr></table></div></div></div><p><u><b>New Export Orders<br /></b></u>Orders and requests for services and other non-manufacturing activities to be provided outside of the U.S. by domestically based companies contracted in October. The New Export Orders Index registered 55.2 percent, up 8.3 percentage points compared to the September reading of 46.9 percent, a return to expansion after one month in contraction. Of the total respondents in October, 40 percent indicated they do not perform, or do not separately measure, orders for work outside of the U.S. Respondent comments include: "Increased demand for subscriptions" and "New service centers offshored."</p><p>The six industries reporting an increase in new export orders in October — in the following order — are: Real Estate, Rental &amp; Leasing; Other Services; Retail Trade; Agriculture, Forestry, Fishing &amp; Hunting; Professional, Scientific &amp; Technical Services; and Utilities. The five industries reporting a decrease in new export orders in October are: Construction; Accommodation &amp; Food Services; Information; Educational Services; and Wholesale Trade. Seven industries reported no change in exports in October.</p><div><div class="divOverflow"><div class="table-responsive"><table><tr><td class="prngen9" colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p class="prnml4"><span class="prnews_span">New Export <br />Orders</span></p></td><td class="prngen10" colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p class="prnml4"><span class="prnews_span">%Higher</span></p></td><td class="prngen10" colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p class="prnml4"><span class="prnews_span">%Same</span></p></td><td class="prngen10" colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p class="prnml4"><span class="prnews_span">%Lower</span></p></td><td class="prngen10" colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p class="prnml4"><span class="prnews_span">Index</span></p></td></tr><tr><td class="prngen9" colspan="1" rowspan="1"><p class="prnml4"><span class="prnews_spa